{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"e0dcdfd1c098ed86","name":"card_unit_pb2y_coronado","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/NavalWarfare/units/card_unit_pb2y_coronado","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"PB2Y CORONADO","text":"Show when drawn: Add a BREWSTER F2A to the support line.\r\nYour fighters have +1 attack.","flavorText":"Consolidated PB2Y Coronado was a large, four-engine flying boat developed for the US Navy and introduced in 1940. It was designed for long-range patrol, bombing and transport roles, and intended as a heavy counterpart to the more famous PBY Catalina. While the Coronado saw limited frontline combat use, it became valuable in the Pacific for long-distance logistics, medical evacuation, and maritime reconnaissance. Early models carried heavy defensive armament and bomb loads, but as the war progressed, many were converted for cargo and troop transport. Some were also outfitted as flying hospital aircraft. Operating from remote island bases, Coronados supported amphibious invasions and strategic airlift across the vast ocean theater. A total of 217 PB2Ys were built, including all variants.","faction":"USA","type":"bomber","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":4,"operationCost":2,"attack":2,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"GameplayTags":["ability.showwhendrawn"],"Name":"card_unit_pb2y_coronado","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_pb2y_coronado_title","SourceString":"PB2Y CORONADO","LocalizedString":"PB2Y CORONADO"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::bomber","attack":2,"defense":4,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_pb2y_coronado_text","SourceString":"Show when drawn: Add a BREWSTER F2A to the support line.\r\nYour fighters have +1 attack.","LocalizedString":"Show when drawn: Add a BREWSTER F2A to the support line.\r\nYour fighters have +1 attack."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_pb2y_coronado_history","SourceString":"Consolidated PB2Y Coronado was a large, four-engine flying boat developed for the US Navy and introduced in 1940. It was designed for long-range patrol, bombing and transport roles, and intended as a heavy counterpart to the more famous PBY Catalina. While the Coronado saw limited frontline combat use, it became valuable in the Pacific for long-distance logistics, medical evacuation, and maritime reconnaissance. Early models carried heavy defensive armament and bomb loads, but as the war progressed, many were converted for cargo and troop transport. Some were also outfitted as flying hospital aircraft. Operating from remote island bases, Coronados supported amphibious invasions and strategic airlift across the vast ocean theater. A total of 217 PB2Ys were built, including all variants.","LocalizedString":"Consolidated PB2Y Coronado was a large, four-engine flying boat developed for the US Navy and introduced in 1940. It was designed for long-range patrol, bombing and transport roles, and intended as a heavy counterpart to the more famous PBY Catalina. While the Coronado saw limited frontline combat use, it became valuable in the Pacific for long-distance logistics, medical evacuation, and maritime reconnaissance. Early models carried heavy defensive armament and bomb loads, but as the war progressed, many were converted for cargo and troop transport. Some were also outfitted as flying hospital aircraft. Operating from remote island bases, Coronados supported amphibious invasions and strategic airlift across the vast ocean theater. A total of 217 PB2Ys were built, including all variants."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::NavalWarfare","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardEnterPlay","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnBeforeOtherCardPlayedFromHand","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardLeaveBoardOrOwner"],"draftBaseWeight":0.9,"spawnCardName":"card_unit_brewster_f2a","Image":{"AssetPathName":"